Collection-window sealing demo ("历史回补" rollback scenario).

Run:

    python examples/windows/backfill.py

The script opens two generations of the same named window using a SQLite
backend, seals the first generation, and then lets old generation-1 work try
to continue its next pipeline step. The output shows which tasks were stopped
in place, which finished before the seal, and which completed in the new
generation. Window state is read back from SQLite after the connection is
closed and reopened.

The demo uses HUEY_WINDOW_DB (default: /tmp/huey-window-demo.db).
